

                   ADVENTURER-KINGS:  GAME 3, TURN 6

                                  FOR

                                 HOKUTO







          Mario Pascoli
          
              
                              




  Quote of the Week:

  John II, King of Poland, after routing the Turks from Vienna in 1683 A.D.:
  "The immortal God... has blest us with so signal a victory as scarce the 
memory of man can equal.  Thanks be to Heaven, now the Half-Moon triumphs no 
longer over the Cross!"


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:

  Stormy winter gave way to sweet spring, and Hokuto made ready to carry out 
his imperial assignments.  He enlisted the 154th Legion and the 155th 
Chariots in St Helens to serve Hokuto.
  With the coming of the early summer season Hokuto cast a Bless spell.  
Cretacia was magically blessed and prospered.  The skeletal remains of the 
247th Legion were Blessed and permanently destroyed.
  Kilkenny was hit by a plague.  The Plague affected no armies in Kilkenny.
  In late summer, Hokuto cast a Bless spell.  Starhaven was magically 
blessed and prospered.  The Bless affected no armies in Starhaven.  His 
experience improved his skill in White Magic.
  Congratulations!  You have attained level 5 in White Magic.  At levels 5 
and up, the usual 15% per level increase in the cast chance is discontinued, 
and the number of spells you can cast in White Magic is capped at 3 Action, 2
Combat.  The effects of the "Holy Symbol" and "Spiritwrack" spells are also 
capped at level 4 (however, skill level will still determine who attacks 
first in personal combat).  Instead, your characters of this exalted level 
gain the following Advanced Ability: 
  WHITE MAGIC- ENHANCED HOLY SYMBOL:  The Holy Symbol spell now has the same 
effect against opponents who have an Evil alignment as it does against 
Undead creatures.

  Starhaven was hit by a plague.  The Plague affected no armies in Starhaven.
  The summer mellowed into the fall.  Hokuto moved into Balmwood (#503) with 
his redoubtable army.  Southeast of here lies the province of Chaco (#504), 
ruled by Kwoth.  It is said to be a Plain province inhabited by Elves.  
Their Elven fighters traditionally fight in the style of Phalanx and 
Heavy Cavalry.  Viewing the southwestern horizon, one can see a Jungle 
province called Katanga (#404).  It is said that Circe reigns there.  It is 
known to be populated by Dwarves.  Their Dwarven warriors fight as Legion 
and Elephants.  Hokuto discovered a previously unknown Glade (#51) in 
Balmwood, held by the Centaur.  Legend says the Large Hoard of Gold is 
hidden here.  Wood-Elves say that the Centaur is a cross-breed, with the 
body of a man and the trunk and legs of a horse.  He is a good archer and is 
usually friendly.
  During early winter, Hokuto boldly marched his forces into Chaco (#504).  
To the east there is a Jungle province known as Ngara (#604), a rich land of 
Humans where Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll reigns.  Their Human 
warriors prefer to array themselves in the style of Legion and Light Cavalry.
Southeast of here is Jerbilia (#605), a prosperous Desert province owned by 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll, where Elves dwell.  Their Elven warriors 
fight in the style of Camel Corps.  Turning to the southwest, one can see a 
prosperous Desert area, which is known as Trouthome (#505).  It is populated 
by Elves and Circe rules there.  Their Elven warriors fight in the style of 
Phalanx.


  A host of warriors carried the banner of 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1) into the Plain province of Chaco, 
ruled by Kwoth (#3).  Uga-Buga Makumb (#1) commanded the attacking armies.  
The defenders were led by Hokuto.  The armies were drawn up into lines of 
battle as shown here:

