  DEFENDING ARMY

  Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll stood determinedly at the head of his 
thousands.  Hokuto marched with his loyal troops, eyes set in grim 
determination.
  Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll strode forward and challenged Hokuto to 
honorable combat.  Hokuto bravely answered the invitation to personal 
combat.  Uga-Buga Makumb chanted his strange words of magic and cast a Gate 
Demon spell and a flaming gate opened, and out of it sprang a terrifying 
demon!
  Hokuto cautiously advanced to bow range.  The Succubus waved her hands and 
gestured rhythmically, meaning to cast a Psychic Blast spell, but it went 
awry and a dove tumbled out of her hat instead.
  Hokuto charged into the melee.  He then thrust at the Succubus but his aim 
was slightly off.  The Succubus assailed Hokuto but her sword whiffed 
harmlessly through the air.
  Showing no fear, Hokuto swang at the Succubus but the Succubus evaded the 
blow.  The Succubus whirled around and thrust at Hokuto and walloped him 
with 6 damage points.  Hokuto swang at his vaunted nemesis and missed.  
The Succubus treacherously swang at Hokuto and would have hit him if Hokuto 
hadn't ducked just then.
  Hokuto acrobatically vaulted over the Succubus and swang at the Succubus 
but his aim was just off.  The Succubus pretended to retreat, then pivoted 
and swang at Hokuto and damaged him, inflicting 1 damage points.  With 
surprising quickness, Hokuto swang at the Succubus but his sword whiffed 
through the air.  Seeking to exploit a gap in his protection, the Succubus 
swang at him but he dodged the blow.  The Succubus swang at Hokuto and 
missed badly.  Hokuto then swang at the Succubus and would have hit 
the Succubus if the Succubus hadn't ducked.
  The Succubus circled left and attacked Hokuto but her aim was slightly off 
the mark.  Hokuto swang at the Succubus and scored on the Succubus, doing 2 
points of damage.  The Succubus whirled about and swang at Hokuto and 
inflicted 1 damage points on him.  Hokuto thrust at his fearsome enemy but 
his sword whiffed through the air.  He feinted one way, then crossed over 
and thrust at the Succubus and inflicted 2 damage points.  The Succubus 
flamboyantly flipped over Hokuto and swang at him and scorched him with 1 
damage points.
  Hokuto pretended to panic, then pivoted and treacherously thrust at 
the Succubus and damaged the Succubus, scoring 5 damage points.  
The Succubus energetically thrust at Hokuto but Hokuto evaded the blow.  
Hokuto swang at the Succubus and missed by a mile.  The Succubus thrust at 
Hokuto and scored on him, inflicting 2 points of damage.
  Hokuto turned away the Succubus with his spirited tactics.  He then thrust 
at the Succubus with maximum force and would have struck the Succubus if 
the Succubus hadn't ducked.  The Succubus angrily attacked Hokuto but her 
aim was slightly off.  Showing no fear, the Succubus moved in and thrust at 
Hokuto but her sword whiffed through the air.  Hokuto audaciously thrust at 
the Succubus and scored 3 damage points on the Succubus.  The Succubus 
thrust at her fearsome enemy but Hokuto evaded the sword.  Hokuto swang at 
the Succubus and inflicted 2 damage points.
  The Succubus flamboyantly vaulted over Hokuto and thrust at him and 
missed.  Hokuto arrogantly thrust at the Succubus and would have hit 
the Succubus if the Succubus hadn't sidestepped just then.  The Succubus 
immediately swang at Hokuto but her aim was slightly off.  Hoping to exploit 
a gap in the Succubus's defenses, Hokuto skillfully swang at the Succubus 
but his sword whiffed through the air.  The Succubus shifted over to a good 
attacking position.  Then the Succubus thrust at Hokuto but Hokuto evaded 
the sword.  Hokuto then thrust at the Succubus with maximum force and 
missed.
  The Succubus circled left and attacked Hokuto and walloped him with 2 
damage points.  Hokuto swang at the Succubus and would have struck 
the Succubus if the Succubus hadn't sidestepped.  The Succubus swang at 
Hokuto and damaged him, scoring 6 damage points.  Hokuto dropped to the 
ground, fatally pierced.  The Succubus disappeared to whence the Succubus 
came.  Thus did Hokuto die, a defiant death by any standard.
  The forces commanded by Hokuto were disheartened by his death, yet still 
they moved ahead with some hope of victory.  (As a result of the encounter, 
"Uga-Buga Makumb" and "Hokuto" have established diplomatic contact.  
"Uga-Buga Makumb" is King #1, Andrea Vitali, ,  ,      , a Elven , Undead 
ruler, (>InterNet:vitello@jopland.org).  
  Uga-Buga Makumb's fortunes took a turn for the better when his scouts 
located a high granite outcropping, which was well suited as an artillery 
site.  Further, his clever tactical maneuvers gave his forces an undeniable 
advantage.

  Out on the right outside wing, the Veteran 316th Bowmen were arrayed 
against the Veteran 282nd Legion.  The 315th Dragons swooped down on the 
267th Chariots and attacked without mercy.  The poor horses of the 267th 
Chariots were spooked by the howls of the terrible Beasts they beheld.  The 
316th Bowmen battled with the 282nd Legion and steadily advanced against 
them.
  In the interior front, the 293rd Dragons were descended upon by the Circle 
of Wraiths, who goaded them into mindless fanatical battle-lust with their 
maniacal laughter.  They faced the Crack 70th Chariots.  The 293rd Dragons 
swooped down on the 70th Chariots and attacked them.  The horses of the 70th 
Chariots were frightened by the fearsome Beasts they beheld.  The horses of 
the 284th Chariots were frightened by the Beasts they were faced with.  In 
this match, the supreme commander condescended to personally ride with the 
troops of the 293rd Dragons in the front lines, inspiring them to a 
surpassing performance.  The 293rd Dragons fought with the 70th Chariots and 
advanced at will.
  Within the interior lines, the 317th Trolls were arrayed against the 
Veteran 71st Legion.  Here, the 71st Legion carelessly stumbled into a nest 
of booby traps and lost some of their best battle-hardened troops.  The 
317th Trolls fought with the 71st Legion and determinedly plowed into their 
opponents.
  In the interior lines, the Veteran 314th Dragons faced the Veteran 283rd 
Legion.  The 314th Dragons swooped down on the 283rd Legion and attacked 
without mercy.  On this battleground, the soldiers of the 314th Dragons 
noticed the presence of an encampment of trollops behind their opponents' 
lines, so they lustily concentrated their efforts to smash through.  The 
outcome seemed bleak for the brave fighters of the 283rd Legion.
  But would victory yet be snatched from the jaws of defeat?  A fantastic 
omen heartened the 283rd Legion.  A flight of silver dragons floated over, 
and their magic mists settled upon the 283rd Legion.  In spite of the 283rd 
Legion's good fortune, the 314th Dragons battled with the 283rd Legion and 
moved ahead slowly, contested for every foot of their advance.
  Out on the left outside wing, the 318th Trolls were arrayed against the 
233rd Chariots.  In this sector, the 233rd Chariots were fearful of defeat.  
But then the 233rd Chariots's regimental high priest picked up his pike and 
joined the battle, and the 233rd Chariots rallied fiercely.  In spite of the 
233rd Chariots's good luck, the 318th Trolls battled the 233rd Chariots and 
steadily advanced against them.
  Uga-Buga Makumb's great horde overwhelmed the army of Kwoth (#3) and took 
the field, scattering their enemies.  The 316th Bowmen demolished the 282nd 
Legion.  The 293rd Dragons slew the 70th Chariots almost to a man.  The 
314th Dragons scattered the 283rd Legion in all directions.  The 315th 
Dragons destroyed the 267th Chariots.  The 293rd Dragons gave chase and 
annihilated the 83rd Camel Corps.  The 314th Dragons overtook the enemy and 
demolished the 155th Chariots.  The 315th Dragons chased after the enemy and 
slew the 284th Chariots almost to a man.
  Uga-Buga Makumb (#1)'s campaign effected the conquest of Chaco.  The 
acting commander withdrew to Balmwood, beaten but not discouraged.
  Thus endeth the adventures of Hokuto for this year.


  Your Majesty, I have news to report of wanderers in our kingdom:  
  Adhemar (#28) heard tales of fine hunting in Tesawa and left Amberleaf to 
have some fun there.
  Ashley (#74) left St Helens to preside over a reunion of his old battalion 
in Balmwood.
  The 212th Camel Corps grew bored with the wines and courtesans of 
Cherrywood and moved on off to Cretacia where they hoped the pickings would 
be more to their liking.


  Here is the financial report for Hokuto's kingdom: this turn, the Kingdom 
collected 52 gold in revenue.  3 gold was expended to finance our leaders.  
The 2nd Light Cavalry, the 154th Legion, the 216th Axemen, the 227th 
Light Cavalry, the 233rd Chariots and the 250th Bowmen trained well and 
improved in quality.  29 gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Hokuto 
was left with 22 gold in the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Ningarl
To: Hokuto

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the advent of the spring season, I set out to quench my thirst for 
adventure.  I marched on Starhaven (#701) with my forces.
  Windy spring was followed by early summer.  I announced a plea for 
recruits in Starhaven and was able to form the 35th Legion, the 47th Legion 
and the 48th Chariots to fight for me.
  In late summer, I moved into Cretacia (#601) with my army.
  With the advent of the fall season I recruited enough men in Cretacia to 
form the 216th Axemen and the 227th Light Cavalry for the army of Ningarl.
  The fall season cooled into early winter.  I cast a Bless spell.  
Amberleaf was magically blessed and prospered.  The Bless affected no armies 
in Amberleaf.

  Thy humble servant,   Ningarl


From: Lexington
To: Hokuto

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Winter melted into spring.  I failed in my attempt to cast a Bless spell.
  In early summer, I cast a Bless spell.  Cretacia was magically blessed and 
prospered.  The skeletal remains of the 69th Legion were Blessed and 
permanently destroyed.
  Midsummer's day came and went and a hot late summer arrived.  I moved into 
Cretacia.
  During fall, I rode into Cherrywood.  I discovered a heretofore unknown 
Dungeon (#81) in Cherrywood, held by the Green Dragon.  Legend says the 
Large Hoard of Gold is hidden here.  The Green Dragon is a powerful dragon 
capable of breathing a poisonous cloud of gas.
  With the advent of the early winter season, I recruited the 250th Bowmen 
and the 2nd Light Cavalry from among the population of Cherrywood, to serve 
under me.  My efforts improved my prowess in Druidism.
  I heard a rumor telling of a perilous feature in Tabora (#705) previously 
unknown to us, a Sacred Rock where dwells the Giant Eagle.  The Sacred Rock 
is reputed to contain the Large Hoard of Gold.

  Thy humble servant,   Lexington


